WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.651
A biopsy removes a small tissue sample.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:09.030
It helps explain what is happening in an organ or an abnormal area.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:11.610
The sample is examined in a laboratory.

00:00:12.079 --> 00:00:17.602
A biopsy can investigate different conditions; it does not automatically mean cancer.

00:00:18.358 --> 00:00:20.434
Our bodies contain organs.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:26.987
Each organ contains different tissues, made up of cells and their surroundings.

00:00:27.693 --> 00:00:30.764
An image reveals an organ's shape.

00:00:31.265 --> 00:00:36.253
A tissue sample adds information about its finer structure.

00:00:36.926 --> 00:00:41.724
The kidneys lie at the back of the abdomen, on either side of the spine below the ribs.

00:00:42.253 --> 00:00:46.996
They filter blood and help balance water and salts.

00:00:47.521 --> 00:00:50.654
Their outer cortex contains many filtering structures.

00:00:51.236 --> 00:00:56.514
A kidney biopsy can reveal inflammation or other tissue damage.

00:00:57.139 --> 00:01:01.498
How the sample is obtained depends on the organ and the question being investigated.

00:01:02.148 --> 00:01:07.512
In a core needle biopsy, a special needle removes a small cylinder of tissue.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:13.076
Ultrasound or other medical imaging can help locate the target.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:17.337
The medical team plans and monitors the procedure.

00:01:18.035 --> 00:01:21.270
The sample is prepared and examined in a laboratory.

00:01:21.676 --> 00:01:26.829
Specialists use a microscope to assess the structure of cells and tissue.

00:01:27.303 --> 00:01:32.723
They may find inflammation, scarring or altered cells.

00:01:33.231 --> 00:01:38.096
The findings are interpreted together with other test results.

00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:43.867
At our station, soft material inside an organ model represents tissue.

00:01:44.366 --> 00:01:48.357
You identify a target and collect a small sample.

00:01:48.865 --> 00:01:54.103
The focus is orientation, controlled movement and careful work.

00:01:54.664 --> 00:02:00.303
The model illustrates the principle of biopsy; real tissue behaves differently.
